.TH MCP-SERVER-SNIPEIT 1 "November 2026" "mcp-server-snipeit 2.0.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
mcp-server-snipeit \- MCP server for the Snipe-IT asset management system
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mcp-server-snipeit
.RB [\|\-\-version \|]
.RB [\|\-\-help \|]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mcp-server-snipeit
is a Model Context Protocol (MCP) server that lets an LLM agent manage a
Snipe-IT instance: assets, consumables, accessories, components, licenses,
users, locations, models, kits, custom fields, imports and reports.
.PP
It speaks MCP over standard input and output and is normally started by an
MCP client or by mcprack rather than by hand.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Print a short help text and exit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SNIPEIT_URL
Base URL of the Snipe-IT instance (required).
.TP
.B SNIPEIT_TOKEN
API token (secret). Required unless OAuth or multi-identity mode is used.
.TP
.B SNIPEIT_READ_ONLY
When "true", every state-changing tool action is refused.
.TP
.B SNIPEIT_ALLOWED_TOOLS
Comma-separated tool allowlist.
.TP
.B MCP_TRANSPORT
"stdio" (default) or "http".
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mcprack (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Upstream: James Gordy. Debian packaging: Vítězslav Dvořák.
